{"name":"Gaslight","hex":"#feffea","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gaslight","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A lamp which operates by burning piped illuminating gas (or town gas).","The light produced by the burning gas in such a lamp."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To manipulate someone such that they doubt their own memory, perceptions of reality, or sanity, typically for malevolent reasons.","To deceive, trick, or lie to."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gaslight"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gas lighting","blocks":[{"text":"Gas lighting is the production of artificial light by burning a fuel gas. Light may be produced directly by the flame or indirectly by heating another material to incandescence, as in a gas mantle or limelight. During the period when gas lighting was widespread, its principal fuel was coal gas; natural gas later replaced coal gas in many places."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Wroc%C5%82aw%2C_ko%C5%9Bci%C3%B3%C5%82_pw._%C5%9B%C5%9B._Piotra_i_Paw%C5%82a_DSCF0144.jpg/330px-Wroc%C5%82aw%2C_ko%C5%9Bci%C3%B3%C5%82_pw._%C5%9B%C5%9B._Piotra_i_Paw%C5%82a_DSCF0144.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gas_lighting","wikidata":"Q856548"},{"title":"Gas Light","blocks":[{"text":"Gas Light is a 1938 thriller play, set in 1880s London, written by the British novelist and playwright Patrick Hamilton. Hamilton's play is a dark tale of a marriage based on deceit and trickery, and a husband committed to driving his wife insane in order to steal from her."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6a/Gas-Light-FE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gas_Light","wikidata":"Q5526304"},{"title":"Gaslight (1944 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Gaslight is a 1944 American psychological thriller film directed by George Cukor, and starring Charles Boyer, Ingrid Bergman, Joseph Cotten and Angela Lansbury in her film debut. Adapted by John Van Druten, Walter Reisch, and John L. Balderston from Patrick Hamilton's play Gas Light (1938), it follows a young woman whose husband slowly manipulates her into believing that she is descending into insanity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Gaslight_%281944_poster%29.jpg/330px-Gaslight_%281944_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaslight_(1944_film)","wikidata":"Q841781"},{"title":"Gaslight (1940 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Gaslight is a 1940 British psychological thriller directed by Thorold Dickinson starring Anton Walbrook, Diana Wynyard and Frank Pettingell. It was written by A. R. Rawlinson and Bridget Boland."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/27/Gaslight_1940_poster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaslight_(1940_film)","wikidata":"Q5526486"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Eclairage.jpg/500px-Eclairage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Eclairage.jpg/1280px-Eclairage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Eclairage.jpg/500px-Eclairage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An illustration of designs of lamplights, c. 1900","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEclairage.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/A_Peep_at_the_Gas_Lights_in_Pall_Mall_Rowlandson_1809.jpg/500px-A_Peep_at_the_Gas_Lights_in_Pall_Mall_Rowlandson_1809.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=th